[{:db/id "q-237031/field-1/be3d012fb37d29051525a627ff26d8aca1bfa7a7dfbd078486f4ffd0dfae0376" :answer/id #uuid "fc55c0b3-1870-5d3e-acd7-aff99013c4d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}x-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-237031/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c46413f9-b558-53bd-9f22-11d016cba92f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-237031/field-1/be3d012fb37d29051525a627ff26d8aca1bfa7a7dfbd078486f4ffd0dfae0376" :answer-field/choices ["q-237031/field-1/be3d012fb37d29051525a627ff26d8aca1bfa7a7dfbd078486f4ffd0dfae0376"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-237031" :question/id #uuid "130d5595-7cbe-51db-aac8-83150d0860ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-237031" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find the equation of the line perpendicular to $y=4x-6$ that passes through the point $(8,-3).$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let ${l}_{1}$ denote the line $y=4x-6,$ and let ${l}_{2}$ denote the line we want to find.\n\nSince perpendicular lines have slopes that are negative reciprocals of each other, the slope of ${l}_{2}$ is the negative reciprocal of the slope of ${l}_{1}.$ Since ${l}_{1}$ has a slope of $4,$ the line ${l}_{2}$ must have a slope of $-\\frac{1}{4}.$\n\nOur perpendicular line must have the slope $m=-\\frac{1}{4}$ and pass through the point $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(8,-3).$ Using point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the equation of the line in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-3) & =-\\frac{1}{4}(x-8) \\\\ y+3 & =-\\frac{1}{4}x+2 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{4}x-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-237031/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae4289af-e251-514c-981e-5c6d21992ad3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-237031"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-44337/selection/3f661a98