on/answer-fields ["q-72567/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "44b9b212-27c4-5d6d-a221-cd85c25fc956"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72567"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72568/selection/d4d9bc559f9b01d432aa8b99354947592794d8d40eec949635221b08b989acf7" :answer/id #uuid "1bb6ad37-ccca-55e6-a371-9cffe47a451f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x+7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72568/selection/1214b4ee03376f049fb9f6c05f73f4bdfec3306e616cc236b05c51f0cfa02fd5" :answer/id #uuid "bc17b0d0-2ec2-56d0-a474-b79cf089d19d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}x-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72568/selection/fd68b447e7d7722e8db1187dcbf8c29c7aee67d7d98213c2d020aea18b6acb58" :answer/id #uuid "a8f80421-001d-5610-9ddd-eaa7f85df628" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72568/selection/ce14a982306b2348c44ef94261c69c82582a07ead14e898ae57ddd0928839170" :answer/id #uuid "a4d7cf86-2019-53c3-bb72-d60df9b3a383" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}x+6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72568/selection/a6d3b12c12e00f4f99d84fb49729cc906a7e405cf80b992b9d33a699ce192513" :answer/id #uuid "a57da595-713d-571f-943c-f851b7f0409d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2x+9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72568/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5948b3b0-f84e-5728-bd08-69af5f4152e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72568/selection/ce14a982306b2348c44ef94261c69c82582a07ead14e898ae57ddd0928839170" :answer-field/choices ["q-72568/selection/d4d9bc559f9b01d432aa8b99354947592794d8d40eec949635221b08b989acf7" "q-72568/selection/1214b4ee03376f049fb9f6c05f73f4bdfec3306e616cc236b05c51f0cfa02fd5" "q-72568/selection/fd68b447e7d7722e8db1187dcbf8c29c7aee67d7d98213c2d020aea18b6acb58" "q-72568/selection/ce14a982306b2348c44ef94261c69c82582a07ead14e898ae57ddd0928839170" "q-72568/selection/a6d3b12c12e00f4f99d84fb49729cc906a7e405cf80b992b9d33a699ce192513"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72568" :question/id #uuid "c5b78a83-fe68-5017-a927-40809114619c" :question/math-academy-id "q-72568" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(-2,5)$ and is perpendicular to the line passing through the points $(6,1)$ and $(4,5).$" :question/worked-solution "Perpendicular lines have slopes which are negative reciprocals of each other.\n\nFirst, let's find the slope ${m}_{1}$ of the line passing through the points $(6,1)$ and $(4,5):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-1}{4-6} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{-2} \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want a perpendicular line, the slope $m$ of the line we're trying to find must satisfy\n\n$$\nm\\cdot (-2)=-1\\,⇒\\,m=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nWe know that the line passes through the point $(-2,5).$ Using point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-5 & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-(-2)) \\\\ y-5 & =\\frac{1}{2}(x+2) \\\\ y-5 & =\\frac{1}{2}x+1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}x+6\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-72568/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "44b9b212-27c4-5d6d-a221-cd85c25fc956"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72568"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-215768/field-1/b00357bbc456f0924a74351e97751af3be7691ec837e17f1b683e5a99f44bd60" :answer/id #uuid "e0735bfe-94a4-58e2-a10b-385d490997ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-215768/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "97e1f251-70da-5c6a-8984-d48773fc9069" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-215768/field-1/b00357bbc456f0924a74351e97751af3be7691ec837e17f1b683e5a99f44bd60" :answer-field/choices ["q-215768/field-1/b00357bbc456f0924a74351e97751af3be7691ec837e17f1b683e5a99f44bd60"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-215768" :question/id #uuid "63ce0ff0-d49c-5492-b89a-ea6a5e332526" :question/math-academy-id "q-215768" :question/is-example false :question/problem "What is the equation of the line that passes through the point $(0,4)$ and is perpendicular to the line passing through the points $(-5,1)$ and $(-6,2)?$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Perpendicular lines have slopes that are negative reciprocals of each other.\n\nFirst, let's find the slope ${m}_{1}$ of the line passing through the points $(-5,1)$ and $(-6,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-1}{-6-(-5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-1}{-6+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-1} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want a perpendicular line, the slope $m$ of the line we're trying to find must satisfy\n\n$$\nm\\cdot (-1)=-1\\,⇒\\,m=1.\n$$\n\nWe know that the line passes through the point $(0,4).$ Using point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the equation of the line in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-4 & =1(x-0) \\\\ y-4 & =x \\\\ y & =x+4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-215768/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "44b9b212-27c4-5d6d-a221-cd85c25fc956"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-215768"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103455/selection/55f854095b797648b52a02afbea29b8bf411207f858cb074c83e2641a6afbb0d" :answer/id #uuid "072f2194-5ab6-5087-a400-4b663f6fdd1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{4}{5}x-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103455/selection/cf4ad43b397e9f7f8faeb76a9ab77189e37ff5913b494a47af63086c8ef49b1b" :ans